{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111776-kinfolk-marriages","id":1111776,"title":"Kinfolk Marriages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-05T12:28:58-07:00","id":1111776,"title":"Kinfolk Marriages","content":"The marriage between two Kinfolk is often one of the most celebrated things among the Garou. Unlike marriages between Garou and Kinfolk, there is no chance of frenzy and, while there is a lower chance of a Garou child, the Kinfolk make up for it by being much more common than the Garou (and there is nothing really stopping married Kinfolk from dallying with Garou whenever Garou are available for breeding other than tribal traditions). I was wondering how you treated Kinfolk marriages, and married Kinfolk, in your games?<br /> <br /> In my games, married Kinfolk are given respect by the Garou because they are acting in an adult fashion to promote the future of the Tribe (the mother determines the Tribe of the Kinfolk in my games, so there are plenty of male Human Kinfolk marrying into other Tribes in my games). While the Garou respect married Kinfolk, they do not believe in monogamy, and married Kinfolk are encouraged to mate with Garou whenever they feel like it (their spouse are encouraged to also mate with Garou for the future of the Tribe). Of course, different Tribes have different traditions, but allowing Kinfolk marriages to be 'open' in relation to Garou is considered to be a necessary adaptation to the limited numbers of the Garou (and means that Garou are required to spend less of their time maintaining a marriage and more of their time killing the servants of the Wyrm). The children of female Garou are given to their female Kinfolk relatives to raise as their own, so the female Garou can return to the fight against the Wyrm as soon as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T13:54:36-07:00","id":1111797,"title":"","content":"I more or less agree, although I'm not so sure about the &quot;most celebrated&quot; part. I view it more as an assumed responsibility of the Kin. My take is that while some Kin bristle a little at the somewhat arrogant expectation that they raise children who are not theirs (Garou who get knocked up and basically dump the kid on the first relatively stable Kinfolk household they find -- or male Kin who have to step aside and raise his spouse's kid who is not biologically his) Nonetheless, most Kin view it as just part of the landscape and any resentment is either offset by the cultural acceptance of that particular situation, or is somewhat atypical. But &quot;celebrated&quot;? No, I disagree with that. When the kid that the Kin have been raising has a First Change -- that's when the Garou celebrate. That's also when the Garou parent comes out of the woodwork and claims the kid (and the Renown). The Kin who raised the (typically socially misfit and increasingly turbulent) kid and were stuck with rebuilding the half of the house the kid ripped down in his First Change Rampage (or whatever consequences arise from the dozen or so dead people in the neighborhood or school), basically get to step back and go &quot;Yay, we... helped?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T16:47:50-07:00","id":1111886,"title":"","content":"I assume it's a pretty common thing which happens all the time and is just like arranged marriages among mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}